## Session Plan — Day 125 (17:25)

**Task 1 (evolve, priority 0 — CI is red):** Root-cause the context.rs fixture-repo flake instead of patching around it again. The #559 failure log is diagnostic: the fixture's second git commit silently failed (file left dirty, no "Recently Changed Files" section) — classic CI env/config leakage (GIT_DIR, gpgsign, hooksPath, missing identity). Fix: fully isolate every fixture git call (GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, `env_remove dangerous vars, inline -c identity/safety), panic loudly with stderr on failure, and assert the postcondition (status --porcelain` clean after commit). This flake has eaten a task and a CI run in 24 hours — it goes first.

